3. Find Missing IDs
Data

1,2,3,5,6,9

Missing → 4,7,8

PySpark:

from pyspark.sql.functions import col, lead
from pyspark.sql.window import Window

w = Window.orderBy("id")

df.withColumn(
    "next_id",
    lead("id").over(w)
).filter(col("next_id") - col("id") > 1)

SQL:

SELECT id+1 AS missing_start,
       next_id-1 AS missing_end
FROM (
    SELECT id,
           LEAD(id) OVER(ORDER BY id) next_id
    FROM numbers
) t
WHERE next_id-id > 1;
